{"duration_api_ms":34119,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"96a35927-93b2-44cf-bcd0-efd67d6fa60a","total_cost_usd":0.1335476,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21236,"cache_read_input_tokens":37778,"output_tokens":4104,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":594},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":21236,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1724,"cache_read_input_tokens":28238,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2538,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2538},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":4104,"cacheReadInputTokens":37778,"cacheCreationInputTokens":21236,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1335476,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":594,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"req-1\",\"requirement\":\"opsadmin configured on node1 with SSH access using the specified ed25519 public key\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"opsadmin user was created, and /home/opsadmin/.ssh/authorized_keys contains exactly the specified public key with correct 700/600 permissions and ownership. Verified both before and after the mandatory restart (boot_id changed from 71f12f87... to e34f7470...), confirming persistence.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-d10621faacd64fe8\",\"cmd-d74a42de7e174dc7\",\"cmd-647ff6edb3d34edf\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2\",\"requirement\":\"Require key-based SSH authentication (disallow password authentication)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"sshd_config was set with PasswordAuthentication no, KbdInteractiveAuthentication no, ChallengeResponseAuthentication no, PubkeyAuthentication yes; sshd -T confirms the effective config both pre- and post-restart. opsadmin's password was locked (shadow entry '!'), and a live SSH attempt to opsadmin@node1 was rejected with only publickey/gssapi offered, both before and after the reboot, demonstrating the control is enforced and persistent.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-d10621faacd64fe8\",\"cmd-42fea6a1be184ccc\",\"cmd-647ff6edb3d34edf\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol on node1 (baseline, restart, boot-identity change, recovered state)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart baseline captured boot_id, uptime, sshd active state, and authorized_keys content. systemctl reboot was issued and acknowledged with stream closure. Polling through connection timeouts/resets confirmed the node went down and came back. Post-restart boot_id (e34f7470...) differs from baseline (71f12f87...) and uptime reflects the new boot time. sshd, opsadmin's key, locked password, and pubkey-only sshd config were all re-verified as intact post-restart, matching the fixed after_executor boot-identity/listening-sockets snapshot cross-check.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-d74a42de7e174dc7\",\"cmd-a0e292a4ba9545f3\",\"cmd-2fd3bc3c67534c0e\",\"cmd-c18506907fbf471b\",\"cmd-9e554e4da4334d45\",\"cmd-64a438553f01470d\",\"cmd-647ff6edb3d34edf\"]}],\"confidence\":0.92,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.8,\"summary\":\"Executor commands were largely purposeful: user/key setup, sshd hardening with a pre-edit backup of sshd_config (a reasonable, low-risk safety practice), password lock, config validation, and a bounded restart-evidence protocol. One minor unnecessary mutation: cmd-42fea6a1be184ccc created /tmp/keytest/id_ed25519 (a placeholder file, not an actual usable private key) during a verification step, and it was never cleaned up — it is still present in the after_executor temporary-files snapshot. This is low-risk residue (a placeholder text file) but was not restored. The sshd_config.bak.<timestamp> backup is also residue in /etc/ssh but represents a defensible operational safety practice before modifying a security-critical config, so it is not penalized as unnecessary. No failed services, no unsafe exposure, and package health remained consistent (dnf) before and after.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-42fea6a1be184ccc\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"Both material outcomes of the task — configuring opsadmin with the specified ed25519 key and enforcing key-based-only SSH authentication — are directly and coherently satisfied by pre- and post-restart evidence, including a live SSH attempt confirming only publickey/gssapi methods are offered. The independent node-restart evidence protocol was also completed correctly with a verified boot-identity change and full recovery of the configured state, corroborated by the fixed lifecycle snapshots. The only blemish is a small leftover placeholder file in /tmp from a verification step that was not cleaned up.\",\"limitations\":[\"No test of an actual private-key SSH login succeeding was performed (executor lacked the corresponding private key), so acceptance of valid pubkey auth is inferred from sshd -T config and denial-of-non-key-auth evidence rather than a successful key login.\",\"The /tmp/keytest/id_ed25519 placeholder residue is low-risk but was left in place rather than cleaned up.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"opsadmin configured on node1 with SSH access using the specified ed25519 public key","status":"satisfied","summary":"opsadmin user was created, and /home/opsadmin/.ssh/authorized_keys contains exactly the specified public key with correct 700/600 permissions and ownership. Verified both before and after the mandatory restart (boot_id changed from 71f12f87... to e34f7470...), confirming persistence.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d10621faacd64fe8","cmd-d74a42de7e174dc7","cmd-647ff6edb3d34edf"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Require key-based SSH authentication (disallow password authentication)","status":"satisfied","summary":"sshd_config was set with PasswordAuthentication no, KbdInteractiveAuthentication no, ChallengeResponseAuthentication no, PubkeyAuthentication yes; sshd -T confirms the effective config both pre- and post-restart. opsadmin's password was locked (shadow entry '!'), and a live SSH attempt to opsadmin@node1 was rejected with only publickey/gssapi offered, both before and after the reboot, demonstrating the control is enforced and persistent.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d10621faacd64fe8","cmd-42fea6a1be184ccc","cmd-647ff6edb3d34edf"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol on node1 (baseline, restart, boot-identity change, recovered state)","status":"satisfied","summary":"Pre-restart baseline captured boot_id, uptime, sshd active state, and authorized_keys content. systemctl reboot was issued and acknowledged with stream closure. Polling through connection timeouts/resets confirmed the node went down and came back. Post-restart boot_id (e34f7470...) differs from baseline (71f12f87...) and uptime reflects the new boot time. sshd, opsadmin's key, locked password, and pubkey-only sshd config were all re-verified as intact post-restart, matching the fixed after_executor boot-identity/listening-sockets snapshot cross-check.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d74a42de7e174dc7","cmd-a0e292a4ba9545f3","cmd-2fd3bc3c67534c0e","cmd-c18506907fbf471b","cmd-9e55